Resource ledger before editing:

Shape: up to 30 caller-controlled values; the current state space is every sum up to `sum(values) // 2`.
Worst case: the list allocation and nested scan are O(n·target) time and O(target) space, with target potentially above 1.5M; this risks the one-second case deadline.
Bound: the required per-case budget is one second; use Python’s sparse bitset integer, giving O(n·target/word_size) effective operations and compact O(target) bits.

Acceptance criteria are: return `False` for odd totals, otherwise detect whether any subset reaches exactly half the total without reusing values, and remain within the supplied timeout for large sums.
